  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Writes the 2-bit value in A into the pixel at pixel_ptr. Call set_pixel_address first. Jump table entry $0915."},
    {"at":10,"placement":"line","text":"Plot vector of the line routine $279e ($2793 puts it in $52/$53). In Mirror mode it inverts the pixel at 4 mirrored points ($281a), else at one point (invert_pixel)."},
    {"at":18,"placement":"line","text":"Inverts both bits of the pixel at pixel_ptr (EOR %11). Call set_pixel_address first."},
    {"at":28,"placement":"line","text":"Shifts the 2-bit value in A to the position of the pixel (pixel_shift) and puts it in pixel_bits. Returns A = the byte at pixel_ptr, Y = 0."},
    {"at":45,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the pixel at X = x (0-159), Y = y (0-199). Returns A = its 2-bit value (0-3)."},
    {"at":52,"placement":"line","text":"Returns A = the 2 bits of the pixel at position X (4 = left, 1 = right) of the byte in A."},
    {"at":63,"placement":"line","text":"Sets pixel_ptr, pixel_mask and pixel_shift for the pixel at X = x (0-159), Y = y (0-199) of the bitmap at $6000. It keeps the line address when Y is the same as before, and does nothing when X and Y are both the same. Returns X = pixel_shift."},
    {"at":73,"placement":"side","text":"Same pixel as before."},
    {"at":111,"placement":"side","text":"Start of the character row Y / 8."},
    {"at":127,"placement":"side","text":"Add the line in the row (Y and 7)."},
    {"at":151,"placement":"side","text":"(X and $fc) * 2 = 8 bytes for each column of 4 pixels."},
    {"at":189,"placement":"line","text":"AND masks that clear pixel 0-3 of a multicolour byte."},
    {"at":193,"placement":"line","text":"Start address of each of the 25 character rows of the bitmap at $6000 ($140 bytes for each row)."}
  ],
